Hi,

On Wednesday 08 December 2010, SourceForge.net wrote:
> the command history() doesn't work for me in rkward (but does in r from the
> command line).
> When I call history() from rkward I get an empty top pane.  The history is
> however saved somewhere, as I can use the arrows to scroll through my
> previous commands. This history is also saved somewhere as I can come back
> to it in a new session of rkward, but I cannot find the file anywhere on
> my computer.  It's not the .Rhistory in my home directory.
> Maybe this is a bug that has been fixed in a newer release, but I can't
> find any mention of it in the forums?

while the R Console in RKWard is meant to behave just like R running in a 
regular console, technically it is quite a different thing. And this means you 
will find a few differences like this in corner cases.

Support for R's history-functions simply has not yet been added, yet. It is on 
our TODO list: 
http://sourceforge.net/tracker/?func=detail&aid=2996587&group_id=50231&atid=459010 
.

Regards
Thomas

P.S.: In RKWard, the history is saved in ~/.kde/share/config/rkwardrc , but 
admittedly not in a form that could be re-used, easily.
